+
+### Rollback
+
+A reviewed forward fix or revert can return node-agent scheduling and its agent-only node-proxy grant to `metal6`, together with the matching original single-worker admission constraint. Remove only the metal3 source from active collector configuration and its log `resourceName`; retain the updated collector image and the existing state PVC. Keep the actual current metal6 Pod pin (refresh through the helper and review if rollout replaced it), rather than restoring a deleted Pod name. The legacy single `agent` input format is also supported, and removed sources' SQLite cursors, observations, identities, incidents and gaps remain retained. Retained historical gaps continue to degrade source status.
+
+Reverting to an old binary is not required to return to single-source operation: its old receipt/history expiry policy would not meet this rollout's preservation boundary. Stop through a reviewed `replicas: 0` change if storage or integrity is uncertain, retain the private database and any rollback journal together after the writer stops, and investigate before resuming. Never delete the PVC, reset SQLite/cursors, purge evidence, force Longhorn attachment/rebuild, alter scanner workloads/CronJobs or enable GitHub publishing. No destructive automated rollback runs. Single-source recovery must verify advancing metal6 reads, retained row counts and an intact database; Homepage coverage may correctly return to 0/2 while its replicas remain on metal3. Keep Gatus process/source checks; the two-source check stays degraded during single-source recovery.
